# Short runs of the systems of the Amber benchmark suite, from 23,558 to
# 1,067,095 atoms, on a GPU in mixed precision: each ends, and every number
# of its log is finite. Counts that differ between the particles and the
# tuples, and rows longer than those of the small tests, reach code that
# the unit tests do not (docs/principles.md, Section 5). The suite runs
# where MDIR_BENCH_DIR holds its prepared inputs
# (scripts/benchmarks/amber/README.md).
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, amber-suite
#
# RUN: %bench --work %amber_suite smoke --mdir mdir | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %bench --work %amber_suite smoke --mdir mdir --analytic-bonds | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: jac_nve: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: jac_nve_4fs: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: jac_npt: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: jac_npt_4fs: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: factorix_nve: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: factorix_npt: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: cellulose_nve: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: cellulose_npt: ok, 2 rows
# CHECK: stmv_npt_4fs: ok, 2 rows
